{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0098","fact_refs":[5],"question":"What method do Hasan and Ng use to model dependent relationships between a post and the post preceding it?","answer":"They use hidden Markov models (HMMs)."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0099","statement":"The model uses an attention mechanism to dynamically decide how much information to use from a word- or character-level component.","source_span":"By using an attention mechanism, the model is able to dynamically decide how much information to use from a word- or character-level component."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0099","statement":"Character-level extensions were found to improve performance on every benchmark tested.","source_span":"character-level extensions were found to improve performance on every benchmark"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0099","statement":"The proposed attention-based architecture delivered the best results even with a smaller number of trainable parameters.","source_span":"the proposed attention-based architecture delivered the best results even with a smaller number of trainable parameters"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0099","statement":"The neural models were evaluated on 8 datasets from the fields of NER, POS-tagging, chunking, and error detection in learner texts.","source_span":"We evaluate the neural models on 8 datasets from the fields of NER, POS-tagging, chunking and error detection in learner texts."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0099","statement":"The base sequence labeling architecture feeds word embeddings into two LSTM components moving in opposite directions through the text, whose outputs are concatenated per word.","source_span":"the embeddings are given as input to two LSTM BIBREF2 components moving in opposite directions through the text, creating context-specific representations. The respective forward- and backward-conditioned representations are concatenated for each word position"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0099","statement":"Label predictions are produced using either a softmax layer or a conditional random field (CRF), with the Viterbi algorithm used to find the optimal label sequence when using the CRF.","source_span":"we use either a softmax layer or a conditional random field (CRF, Lafferty2001)... the Viterbi algorithm is used to find an optimal sequence of weights"}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0099","fact_refs":[3],"question":"On how many datasets, and from which NLP tasks, were the sequence labeling models evaluated in this paper?","answer":"They were evaluated on 8 datasets from the fields of NER, POS-tagging, chunking, and error detection in learner texts."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0099","fact_refs":[1],"question":"What effect did adding character-level extensions have across the benchmarks tested?","answer":"Character-level extensions were found to improve performance on every benchmark tested."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0099","fact_refs":[0],"question":"How does the model decide how much to rely on word-level versus character-level representations for a word?","answer":"It uses an attention mechanism that dynamically decides how much information to use from the word- or character-level component."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0099","fact_refs":[2],"question":"Besides achieving the best results, what other advantage did the attention-based architecture have?","answer":"It achieved the best results while requiring a smaller number of trainable parameters."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0099","fact_refs":[4],"question":"How does the base sequence labeling model build a context-specific representation from the input word embeddings?","answer":"It feeds the embeddings into two LSTM components that move in opposite directions through the text, then concatenates the forward- and backward-conditioned representations for each word position."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0099","fact_refs":[5],"question":"What two options are described for the output layer that produces label predictions, and what algorithm is used to find the optimal label sequence for one of them?","answer":"The output layer can be either a softmax layer or a conditional random field (CRF); when using the CRF, the Viterbi algorithm finds the optimal sequence of labels."}
